# Whether a variable of the file that a loop reads anew in each turn is told apart in front of the loop is asked of the loop's own text: does it compare the variable's elements with characters? An element
# with a name and two comparisons, relations, and a switch say so as one `===` does. A character is a text of one unit, whatever the number of its bytes.
# f1 = named, f2 = between, f3 = switched
# RUN(NAMED): walk f1:Body mechanisms=all
# NAMED: = GetStringCodeUnit
# RUN(BETWEEN): walk f2:Body mechanisms=all
# BETWEEN: = GetStringCodeUnit
# RUN(SWITCHED): walk f3:Body mechanisms=all
# SWITCHED: = GetStringCodeUnit
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell globalThis.sink = () => {};
# ANSWERS: 4,5,5 2 1 2
